# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same variable in the
# Vercel project's Environment Variables for the deployment.
#
# SESSION_SECRET encrypts each user's Academia session before it's stored in
# their own httpOnly cookie (see lib/auth/session-crypto.ts). The server keeps
# no copy of any session, so this key is the only thing protecting them.
#
# Generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Rules:
#   - Must be at least 32 characters. Shorter values are rejected at startup.
#   - NEVER commit the real value. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
#   - Use a DIFFERENT secret for production than for local development.
#   - Rotating it logs every user out (their cookies stop decrypting). That is
#     the intended way to force a global sign-out.
SESSION_SECRET=replace-me-with-openssl-rand-hex-32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: per-IP rate limiting on the login form (lib/auth/rate-limit.ts).
#
# Strongly recommended before making the app public. /login forwards every
# submission to Zoho, so without a limit someone can both brute-force SRM
# accounts through this deployment AND get its IPs throttled by Zoho, which
# breaks sign-in for everyone.
#
# Setup (free tier is far more than enough):
#   1. Create a Redis database at https://console.upstash.com
#   2. Copy the "REST API" URL and token from its dashboard
#   3. Paste them below, and add both to the Vercel project's env vars
#
# If these are unset the app still runs — the limiter fails OPEN (allows
# logins) rather than blocking sign-in over a missing optional dependency.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
